Expected elements: present

Presence check, done first and carefully. Identity bar: `← aztec` (exit to the chain — correct, not a finding), `0xb63616…6359`, `Partial`, `block 101`, both stepping directions (◀ ▶ plus in/out, jump and end pairs), a scrubber track with a cyan fill and thumb at ~10%, the position readout `128 / 1315` beside it as a separate element, and the `FETCHING OPENING POSITIONING` rail. Scrubber and readout are both present and both legible at this width. `CODE` with the current position on line 32; `CALL TRACE | EVENT LOG` as one tab strip with Call Trace open; seven frames; `VALUES` with ten rows; `TRANSACTION`. No provenance band above the bar — provenance is the `DATA` row of the Transaction pane, badge `Synthetic demo data`, producer's sentences beneath. Nothing forbidden present.

The type system is coherent: one tracked all-caps pane-title level, one monospace face for code and values, tabular right-aligned ACIR and value columns across four magnitudes.

Below bar: the provenance paragraph is set flush-right over thirteen lines at a ~24-character measure — thirteen ragged line-starts for the page's most important sentence. The code listing's row pitch is not constant: 23px normally, 41–44px wherever an inline value badge wraps to its own row (26→27, 48→49, 49→50), so the line-number column stops being an even ruler. FEE PAYER and TARGET wrap 64-character hashes across three lines and leave two-character orphans (`32`, `4c`) where the identity bar uses ellipsis truncation.

Fixes: set the DATA paragraph flush-left; keep one row pitch in the listing and clip badges to the line.

Rating: 6/10

